{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-4630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x-3}{2{x}^{2}-x-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-4630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x-3}{2{x}^{2}-x-1} & =\\frac{(x-1)(x+3)}{(2x+1)(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-1)}(x+3)}{(2x+1)\\cancel{(x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+3}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n2x+1=0\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-4630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd3e3d7030c59e7553bf6f3b3dde4cf673078e85e547dc5b6f76bc8dc123ab36"} {"question" "q-4630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-4630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-1,\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x=-3,\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,x=1"] ["text" "No vertical asymptotes"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-4630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-37070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x}{8x-6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-37070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x}{8x-6} & =\\frac{x(4x-3)}{2(4x-3)}=\\frac{x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/assets/3e6ebc8eaec86276442b13fde934234fdaf9c4a457398bb1b792c6910350e44c.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-37070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd3e3d7030c59e7553bf6f3b3dde4cf673078e85e547dc5b6f76bc8dc123ab36"} {"question" "q-37070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-37070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=6"] ["math" "x=\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{3}{8}"] ["text" "No vertical asymptotes"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-37070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No vertical asymptotes"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}-\\frac{1}{x-6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x+3}-\\frac{1}{x-6} & =\\frac{x-6-(x+3)}{(x+3)(x-6)}=-\\frac{9}{(x+3)(x-6)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n(x+3)(x-6)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-3\\,,\\,x=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=-3$ and $x=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd3e3d7030c59e7553bf6f3b3dde4cf673078e85e547dc5b6f76bc8dc123ab36"} {"question" "q-73029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-3"] ["math" "x=3"] ["math" "x=6"] ["text" "$x=-3$, $x=6$"] ["text" "$x=-6$, $x=3$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-3$, $x=6$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x+1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x+1} & =\\frac{x+1+(x-1)}{(x-1)(x+1)}=\\frac{2x}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n(x-1)(x+1)=0\\,⟹\\,x=1\\,,\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=1$ and $x=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd3e3d7030c59e7553bf6f3b3dde4cf673078e85e547dc5b6f76bc8dc123ab36"} {"question" "q-73031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-1"] ["math" "x=0"] ["math" "x=2"] ["text" "$x=1$, $x=-1$"] ["text" "$x=\\frac{1}{2}$, $x=1$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-73031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=1$, $x=-1$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-107028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{4x-12}{3{x}^{2}-9x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-107028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-12}{3{x}^{2}-9x} & =\\frac{4(x-3)}{3x(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cancel{(x-3)}}{3x\\cancel{(x-3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n3x=0\\,⟹\\,x=0\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-107028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd3e3d7030c59e7553bf6f3b3dde4cf673078e85e547dc5b6f76bc8dc123ab36"} {"question" "q-107028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/state.json" "file_sha256" "1aaf9929f44c63d8ef1c55cb2f09272c567509429c82b403054936ed11fad300"} {"question" "q-107028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=0"] ["math" "x=3"] ["math" "x=4"] ["text" "$x=0$, $x=3$"] ["text" "$x=0$, $x=4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Develo